biệt rõ với nghĩa trạng thái hoặc cấu hình đã sẵn sàng.","review_status":"COMPLETE","review_vote_sha256":"c3f8ada93b649f27fce2906e87278af44e04dd09844c43fc4d09515f97fd93e7","reviewer_slot":"reviewer_2","scope_decision":"ACCEPT","split_decision":"ACCEPT_SPLIT"},{"candidate_set_decision":"ACCEPT","context_evidence_decision":"ACCEPT","corrected_definition_en":"","corrected_part_of_speech":"","corrected_scope":"","definition_decision":"ACCEPT","part_of_speech_decision":"ACCEPT","review_input_sha256":"689501d471bd0569e50d8fdd7d7e106f7f8a3a20891f634975bd19455a98d61c","review_notes":"All 5 contexts (ndarray b091/b092/b099/b104, hybridize b064) describe mutating an existing array/parameter/memory location in place rather than allocating a replacement, matching the proposed definition and scope ARRAY_OR_PARAMETER_UPDATE_ON_EXISTING_STORAGE. This sense is clearly distinct from the ESTABLISHED_CONFIGURATION sense of the same parent (readiness/being in effect, e.g. 'algorithm currently in place'), so splitting the parent is well supported by the corpus -> ACCEPT_SPLIT. POS 'adverb' is an acceptable simplification for this idiomatic phrase even though a few instances (e.g. 'in-place operations') read attributively; the taxonomy has no separate idiom/adjective-adverb hybrid tag. Candidates 'tai cho', 'cap nhat tai cho', and 'truc tiep tren doi tuong hien co' are three distinct, defensible glosses.","review_status":"COMPLETE","review_vote_sha256":"657ae4fd2a7397c5393d9aa346256eeeccd0af1d7681b6ae2f62f3ddc4f12c33","reviewer_slot":"reviewer_3","scope_decision":"ACCEPT","split_decision":"ACCEPT_SPLIT"}],"schema_id":"D2LTargetedRepairReviewConsensusV1","schema_version":"1.0.0","source_payload_sha256":"7a440e1c56daf96737c6d968e7af3ee6130eb4bbb93cffcec7d11e199fad0e2d","source_term":"in place","split_label":"IN_PLACE_MUTATION"}
